<p class="lead">
  "Flatten this PDF" is common instruction in form-filling and document workflows, and it's not always obvious what it actually changes. The short version: it converts something editable into something fixed.
</p>

<h2>Flatten a PDF in your browser (no upload, free)</h2>
<p>
  The <a href="/tools/flatten-pdf/">Flatten PDF tool</a> on keptlocal locks form fields — and optionally annotations — into permanent page content, entirely on your device.
</p>
